<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Civic Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1987–1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Cruzada Civilista Nacional</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Civic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> (Cruzada Civilista Nacional) was a Panamanian opposition movement formed in June 1987 by business, professional and church groups against the military regime of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega">Manuel Noriega</a>. It arose after the former chief of staff Roberto Díaz Herrera accused Noriega of rigging the 1984 election and ordering the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-spadafora">Hugo Spadafora</a>. Its mass protests and general strikes were met with repression and continued until the American invasion of 1989.</p></div>
